# Test corpus (task 06.0): sanitized, captured third-party HTML is machine-generated.
# Mark it linguist-generated and suppress textual diffs so pull-request reviews stay
# readable and GitHub does not count it as hand-written source.
#
# Threat model FIX-13: suppressing the HTML diff must NOT become a review-bypass. The
# compensating controls are (a) tests/unit/test_fixture_corpus.py::test_meta_sha256_matches_file,
# which fails if any .html is edited after capture, (b) the secret-scan gate run over
# tests/fixtures/, and (c) goldens (*.expected.json) staying fully diffable below.
tests/fixtures/**/*.html linguist-generated=true -diff

# Golden records stay diffable and reviewable - a deliberate golden change must show
# up in the PR diff.
tests/fixtures/**/*.expected.json -linguist-generated diff
